        "t": "chr",
        "v": [
          "This module assesses whether the paper's code could be run on its data, and — because `execute = TRUE` — **actually ran it**. We examined 2 R code files.",
          "#### Run order",
          "No ordering signal (no data dependency, `source()` call, or numeric filename prefix) distinguishes the run order of these files. They may need to run in a specific order that could not be determined automatically — check this before running.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Order = 1:2, File = c(\"needs_missing_pkg.R\", \"ok.R\"\n), \"Runs after\" = c(\"—\", \"—\"), Basis = c(\"none\", \"none\")), row.names = c(NA, \n-2L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### File paths",
          "Every data path in the code works in the repository as deposited.",
          "#### Execution",
          "**The code was run.** Each script ran in an isolated Docker container against a throwaway copy of the repository, in the run order above, with a 60-second per-script timeout. Of 2 scripts: 1 ran without error, 0 errored, 0 timed out, 1 could not run because one of its own dependencies is unavailable, 0 did not parse. Running against current package versions: a break can reflect version drift, which argues for pinning versions.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = c(\"needs_missing_pkg.R\", \"ok.R\"), Outcome = c(\"dependency_unavailable\", \n\"ran_ok\"), Detail = c(\"dependency_unavailable\", \"\"), \"Time (s)\" = 0), row.names = c(NA, -2L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 15, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "**Dependency-unavailable errors**",
          "**1 script could not run because its own dependency is unavailable** — the package failed to install from both live CRAN and the CRAN Archive (or a GitHub/URL source could not be resolved). This is an infrastructure limitation, not a defect in the paper's code, so it does **not** force the traffic light red.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"needs_missing_pkg.R\"), row.names = c(NA, \n-1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "*Expand a row below to see the output each script produced.*",
          "::: {.callout-tip title=\"Output — needs_missing_pkg.R (dependency_unavailable)\" collapse=\"true\"}\n\n**Output (stdout):**\n````\n> library(notapkg123)\n````\n**Messages / errors (stderr):**\n````\nError in library(notapkg123) : there is no package called ‘notapkg123’\n````\n\n:::\n",
          "::: {.callout-tip title=\"Output — ok.R (ran_ok)\" collapse=\"true\"}\n\n**Output (stdout):**\n````\n> dat <- read.csv(\"data.csv\")\n> t.test(dat$x ~ dat$g)\n\n\tWelch Two Sample t-test\n\ndata:  dat$x by dat$g\nt = -4.0415, df = 4.9592, p-value = 0.01008\nalternative hypothesis: true difference in means between group a and group b is not equal to 0\n95 percent confidence interval:\n -5.731711 -1.268289\nsample estimates:\nmean in group a mean in group b \n            2.0             5.5 \n````\n\n:::\n",
          "Dependencies were installed into a throwaway library before running: 2 succeeded, 2 failed. notapkg123, oldpkg, oddpkg, fine were installed.",
          "**1 of these were no longer on live CRAN** and were instead installed from the **CRAN Archive**'s most recent published version — a real version the package once had, but not necessarily the one the paper's authors used: oldpkg.",
          "**Failed:** notapkg123 [not available on CRAN for this R version] (package is not available for this version of R); oddpkg [NA] (NA)"
